---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Migrate from Mint to Wicker Money"
  description="Moving from Mint to a self-hosted app: what Wicker Money's CSV import handles today, and what isn't built yet (there is no bank sync)."
>
  <section class="wmm-section wmm-page-hero">
    <div class="wmm-container">
      <p class="wmm-eyebrow">Coming from Mint</p>
      <h1>Bringing your data over</h1>
      <p class="wmm-lede">
        Mint shut down and took its "just works" bank sync with it. Wicker Money doesn't
        replace that experience yet — here's exactly what it does today, so you can
        decide if it's worth the manual step right now.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wmm-section wmm-section--alt">
    <div class="wmm-container">
      <h2>What's actually built today</h2>
      <p class="wmm-lede" style="max-width: 72ch;">
        Wicker Money imports from CSV. There's no automatic bank sync yet — that's not
        on the roadmap as a near-term item, so if a live bank connection is a
        dealbreaker for you right now, this isn't ready for that yet. What the CSV
        importer does handle:
      </p>
      <ul class="wmm-checklist">
        <li>A saved column mapping per source, so re-importing from the same bank later doesn't mean re-mapping columns every time.</li>
        <li>An explicit date format with a live parse preview, instead of guessing and hoping.</li>
        <li>Duplicate detection across imports.</li>
        <li>Category rules with a preview before a rule touches anything, plus triage for whatever a rule doesn't catch.</li>
        <li>Batch undo, if an import or a rule does something you didn't want.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wmm-section">
    <div class="wmm-container">
      <h2>The path</h2>
      <ol class="wmm-steps wmm-steps--wide">
        <li>
          <strong>Get your history out.</strong> If you still have an old Mint export
          sitting around, start there. Going forward, each bank and card issuer has its
          own CSV export — that's what feeds Wicker Money from here on, one account at
          a time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Set up your accounts and categories in Wicker Money first.</strong>
          Decide your category list before the first big import; it's easier to import
          into categories that already exist than to rename hundreds of transactions
          after the fact.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Import one account, map its columns once.</strong> The mapping is
          saved per source, so the next statement from the same account is a straight
          re-import.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Write a handful of category rules, then triage what's left.</strong>
          Rules preview before they apply, so you can see what a rule will do before it
          touches your ledger.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Tell it what's coming.</strong> Add your paychecks and regular
          bills on the Recurring page. The &ldquo;Until payday&rdquo; widget then
          shows what's safe to spend before your next paycheck, and the Forecast
          shows where each account is heading. When a bill posts, confirm the
          suggested match so it isn't counted twice.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wmm-section wmm-section--alt">
    <div class="wmm-container">
      <h2>Still deciding?</h2>
      <p class="wmm-lede" style="max-width: 72ch;">
        See <a href="/features">what's built versus planned</a> for the honest current
        state, or go straight to <a href="/self-hosting">self-hosting</a> if the manual
        import above is a trade you're fine making for owning your data.
      </p>
      <div class="wmm-btn-row">
        <a class="wmm-btn wmm-btn--primary" href="/self-hosting">Set up self-hosting</a>
        <a class="wmm-btn wmm-btn--secondary" href="/features">What's built vs. planned</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .wmm-checklist {
      list-style: none;
      padding: 0;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 10px;
      max-width: 68ch;
    }
    .wmm-checklist li {
      padding-left: 28px;
      position: relative;
      color: var(--wm-text-muted);
    }
    .wmm-checklist li::before {
      content: '\2713';
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
      color: var(--wm-positive);
      font-weight: 700;
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
